# Build output
build/
testbench/build/
testbench/framecache/
testbench/external/miniaudio.h

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime logs
*.log

# Raw capture video (hundreds of MB; CSV/YAML sidecars are kept)
*.mp4

# Vanilla Skyrim audio staged for auditioning in assets\sfx\skyrim\ (see its README).
# Bethesda's assets, so the audio stays out of the repo; the survey that gives it its
# value - manifest.csv and README.md - is ours and stays tracked. Matched on the prefix
# rather than the folder so a stray copy is caught anywhere, including assets\sfx\library\
# where it would otherwise deploy. Extensions are the set SfxLibrary indexes (Sfx.cpp:30).
skyrim_*.wav
skyrim_*.mp3
skyrim_*.ogg
skyrim_*.flac

# ...and the sidecar the importer writes beside a local copy of one. It is our
# measurement rather than Bethesda's audio, but it measures a file that is never
# in the repo, so tracking it would leave 35 readings of nothing. The survey that
# is worth keeping is assets\sfx\skyrim\manifest.csv.
skyrim_*.meta.ini
